Z||000000||turbo86se||07-27-2001||02:11 PM||||The man's name was Casey, real nice guy. The low-mileage black '87GT wasn't his, it was his mother's. He said his family has 3 Fieros. <BR>I did the old park next to the Fiero trick, too bad I was in my '00 Altima! I did have the recovered seats I just picked up for my '88 coupe in the back seat! I have him a FOCOSEVA card and told him of the Forum, hopefully he'll drop in here!!<P>Casey did have really cool personalized tags: MSBHAVIN <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||varnster||07-27-2001||06:23 PM||||Thats cool, there are quiet a few owners in tn, but you hardly ever see one on the road,<BR>but the bone yards are full! My only problem<BR>is there all notch back 4 cylinders, I have<BR>yet to see any fastbacks,and only 1 gt, and <BR>I travel all over the state.||||reg||9
Z||000002||Songman||07-27-2001||10:48 PM||||Did he say where he was from in TN? We need to get him in the club too..<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||8Ball||07-28-2001||08:49 AM||||There are 2 fastback GT's on my street.<BR>I almost bought the 88 gt about a year ago but he wanted a little more than I was willing to give at the time. I think he was asking 6k then and the interior was trashed.<P> He has since taken it off the market and started fixing it back up<P>8ball||||reg||1
